<title>LITHUANIA: THE BOURSE DECIDED TO LIST SEVEN NEW ISSUES.</title>
<headline>THE BOURSE DECIDED TO LIST SEVEN NEW ISSUES.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of Lithuania's stock</p>
<p>exchange said on Tuesday that it decided to list the ordinary</p>
<p>shares of seven companies on the current list of the Vilnius</p>
<p>bourse and to allow transactions with them from August 18.</p>
<p>				 Number    Face value   Face value</p>
<p>				 of shares of share     of the issue</p>
<p>    - Mazheikiu Pienine  4,404,142   1	    4,404,142</p>
<p>    - Parnario Aitvaras    470,473   10	   4,704,730</p>
<p>    - Morena		 2,256,056   1	    2,256,056</p>
<p>    - Rizgonys	     2,831,171   1	    2,831,171</p>
<p>    - Raista		    12,794   40	     511,760</p>
<p>    - Tilremas		  39,097   10	     390,970</p>
<p>    - Litimpeks Bank    60,000,000   1	   60,000,000</p>
<p>The bourse said in a statement that Litimpeks Bank's shares</p>
<p>will only be traded in block transations.</p>
<p>It also said that the financial situation of Tilremas and</p>
<p>Litimpeks Bank should be taken into account since they reported</p>
<p>losses for the first half of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
